yle":{"color":"var(--color-muted-foreground)","size":8,"opacity":1}},{"id":"L4-0","layer":4,"position":0,"style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","size":8,"opacity":1}},{"id":"L4-1","layer":4,"position":1,"style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","size":8,"opacity":1}},{"id":"L4-2","layer":4,"position":2,"style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","size":8,"opacity":1}},{"id":"L4-3","layer":4,"position":3,"style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","size":8,"opacity":1}},{"id":"L4-4","layer":4,"position":4,"style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","size":8,"opacity":1}},{"id":"L4-5","layer":4,"position":5,"style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","size":8,"opacity":1}}],"addEdges":[{"from":"L2-0","to":"L3-0","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L2-0","to":"L3-1","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L2-0","to":"L3-2","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L2-4","to":"L3-3","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted-foreground)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L2-4","to":"L3-4","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L2-4","to":"L3-5","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted-foreground)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L3-3","to":"L4-0","style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","strokeWidth":1.5,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L3-3","to":"L4-1","style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","strokeWidth":1.5,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L3-3","to":"L4-2","style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","strokeWidth":1.5,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L3-5","to":"L4-3","style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","strokeWidth":1.5,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L3-5","to":"L4-4","style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","strokeWidth":1.5,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L3-5","to":"L4-5","style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","strokeWidth":1.5,"opacity":1}}],"setText":"Time for the combination lock. The agent tries 6 different ways of translating the chain \"GEAR → mechanism A → Lightbulb\" into the final code. Click.","setCode":"@encompass.compile\ndef solve_escape_room():\n    ...\n    branchpoint()\n    code = solve_combination(cipher, logic, riddle)\n    success = open_door(code)\n    record_score(success)\n","highlightLines":[4]},{"addNodes":[{"id":"L3-3","layer":3,"position":3,"style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","size":8,"opacity":1}},{"id":"L4-0","layer":4,"position":0,"style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","size":8,"opacity":1}},{"id":"L4-1","layer":4,"position":1,"style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","size":8,"opacity":1}},{"id":"L4-2","layer":4,"position":2,"style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","size":8,"opacity":1}},{"id":"L4-3","layer":4,"position":3,"style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","size":8,"opacity":1}},{"id":"L4-4","layer":4,"position":4,"style":{"color":"var(--color-brand-secondary)","size":16,"opacity":1}},{"id":"L4-5","layer":4,"position":5,"style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","size":8,"opacity":1}}],"addEdges":[{"from":"L2-4","to":"L3-3","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L2-4","to":"L3-5","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted-foreground)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L3-3","to":"L4-0","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L3-3","to":"L4-1","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L3-3","to":"L4-2","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L3-5","to":"L4-3","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L3-5","to":"L4-4","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted-foreground)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}},{"from":"L3-5","to":"L4-5","style":{"color":"var(--color-muted)","strokeWidth":1,"opacity":1}}],"setText":"The lock opens and the door swings wide. The agent has escaped!","highlightLines":[7]}]},"loop":false,"autoPlay":false,"showControls":true,"caption":"$L46"}]
21:["$","p",null,{"children":["At runtime, you can tell ",["$","span",null,{"className":"","style":{"fontVariant":"small-caps"},"children":"EnCompass"}]," which search strategy to use and it automatically manages the execution. For example, the animation above shows beam search using a beam width of 2 and a branching factor of 3. ",["$","span",null,{"className":"","style":{"fontVariant":"small-caps"},"children":"EnCompass"}]," samples 3 different cipher decodings at the first branchpoint, scores each of them, and keeps the top 2 options. At the logic puzzle, it generates 3 attempts for both cipher paths (6 total), scores them, and keeps only the 2 highest-scoring combinations."]}]
22:["$","p",null,{"children":["When one path reaches the riddle and fails, the other paths continue exploring. ",["$","span",null,{"className":"","style":{"fontVariant":"small-caps"},"children":"EnCompass"}]," might find success through a cipher interpretation that scored slightly lower initially but leads to a correct riddle answer. Other search strategies may handle exploration differently. While beam search maintains multiple parallel paths, ",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monte_Carlo_tree_search","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"external-link-in-content","children":"Monte-Carlo Tree Search (MCTS)"}]," repeatedly explores and expands the tree of future actions from a given decision point."]}]
23:["$","p",null,{"children":["The key advantage with ",["$","span",null,{"className":"","style":{"fontVariant":"small-caps"},"children":"EnCompass"}]," is that you can swap between these distinct strategies without changing a single line of the core escape room code. The workflow stays clean and readable because the framework handles all the complex search logic behind the scenes."]}]
24:["$","h2",null,{"id":"code-translation-case-study","children":"Code translation case study"}]
25:["$","p",null,{"children":["We applied ",["$","span",null,{"className":"","style":{"fontVariant":"small-caps"},"children":"EnCompass"}]," to several practical tasks to validate these improvements. Similar to the escape room example, these tasks all involved sequential steps with dependencies and uncertainty. Across our case studies, implementing search strategies at inference time (when the agent runs) required three to six times fewer lines of code changes with ",["$","span",null,{"className":"","style":{"fontVariant":"small-caps"},"children":"EnCompass"}]," compared to standard Python implementations."]}]
26:["$","$L47",null,{"caption":["Code modifications to implement search in our case studies, without"," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"","style":{"fontVariant":"small-caps"},"children":"EnCompass"}]," versus with"," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"","style":{"fontVariant":"small-caps"},"children":"EnCompass"}]," (highlighted). Metrics include the number lines/words added, changed, and removed, the number of new function definitions, and the number of lines of the original code where the indentation level was changed. For context, we also give the number of lines of code used to implement the core logic of the original base agent."]}]
27:["$","p",null,{"children":["Beyond code efficiency, ",["$","span",null,{"className":"","style":{"fontVariant":"small-caps"},"children":"EnCompass"}]," enables clearer, more maintainable code. To see how, consider a simplified version of a Java-to-Python translation agent that iterates through source functions, translating and testing each one using an LLM."]}]
28:["$","p",null,{"children":["Without ",["$","span",null,{"className":"","style":{"fontVariant":"small-caps"},"children":"EnCompass"}],", one way to support general search strategies over this agent’s workflow is to use a state machine. The states track locations in the workflow, i.e., beginning to translate a function or beginning to test a function. Transitions between states implement steps of the workflow such as translating and testing a specific function in the codebase."]}]
